gration keeps my workplace and my community going. Cutting it back would cost us more than it would save.","22":"Migration is about people, not just workers. Families being able to live together should count as much as economic contribution.","27":"If we expect newcomers to learn English, classes and settlement support should be funded for everyone, not just permanent arrivals.","31":"The culture of my community is changing faster than people can adjust, and it’s fair to worry about that.","34":"As a lucky country, we have a duty to keep helping people who aren’t so lucky, even when it costs us.","61":"International students add to the quality of Australian education by bringing different perspectives.","66":"People would support our migration system more if it was acknowledged that there are some countries which we should not take migrants from","69":"A temporary visa should not lead to permanent residency.","86":"Why can’t family reunions can take place in the country of origin, why should the Australian taxpayer fund someone’s family to come here?","95":"Migrants are not the problem with the housing market","96":"Migrants bring valued traditions to our communities","98":"Helping families reunite is an important part of a working migration shstem","103":"Without migration the economic burden to provide for an ageing population will fall to fewer people.","107":"If Australia had the infrastructure and resources for a larger population, would you support a higher net migration?","109":"The process for family migration, in particular for older parents joining their Australian citizen children needs to be quicker and clearer","113":"Anti migration sentiment is unfortunately always targeted at black / brown skin tones.","122":"I don’t have a problem with genuine refugees provided they are vetted but I do have a problem with assylum seekers being given a free run.","123":"The migration debate seems to have become more racist and less trusted since cost-of-living became a real issue here.","131":"If there is a housing shortage, is immigration fuelling an increase in house prices and so the affordability crisi we hear about?","134":"Migration has worked well and should be seen as a positive","144":"Migrants have enhanced our culture and economy.","165":"Migrant crime is a real issue and threatening to our way of life","169":"There are too many new migrants coming in we need to shut the gates and focus on remigration of the illegal ones","171":"Mass migration is destroying social cohesion, we need a 5 year pause on all migration","176":"Australians should not forget we are all migrants except for First Nations people as so deal with newer migrants humanely","178":"All too often migrants are blamed for the difficulties people experience during challenging times.","179":"Offshore detention should be abolished and asylum seekers should work in shortage areas while applications are processed","198":"Social benefits should only apply to citizens.","224":"Migrants on visas should have access to services like medicare","249":"When bringing in people from trouble spots, we need to fund extra support to help them settle.","294":"the government needs to be extracting money from large multinational corporations not migrants and international students","392":"Shelter is a basic human right, and if our kids cannot buy/rent their own homes, the immigration numbers need to be reduced drastically"},"nsplit":40,"allies":"bbvvbbvvbvvvvvbvbbbvvbvbvbvbbbvvvbbbbbvv-vvbvbvbvbbvbvvbbbvb-vvb-v--bvvb-----vbb-vbv--b---v--b-b--v--b------bb-b--v-v--b-b--b-b---------vvv--v----v-b------------------------v----------------vv---b-----------------v---bv---b-----v--b","cut":0.427};
